<title>USA: Vermont House rejects pay rises without debate.</title>
<headline>Vermont House rejects pay rises without debate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vermont House has rejected a plan that would have granted lawmakers future pay raises without debate.</p>
<p>Legislators are prohibited from raising their own pay directly, but do vote on pay for the next session.</p>
<p>The bill rejected by the House would have automatically increased pay whenever unionized state employees negotiated a pay raise. Opponents say how much lawmakers pay themselves should be the subject of open debate, and a recorded vote.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
